  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656586",
      "title": "Pure and Impure Pipes (or: How to \"fix\" the Filter Pipe)",
      "lectureOrder": 573,
      "videoOrder": 526,
      "sourceHash": "068de59536ed96c0e5846fe3dbbd32a38d886cf1290b285f3715b87c7c864281",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.11,
          "end": 5.07,
          "en": "-: In the last video, we created this filter pipe here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.07,
          "end": 8.01,
          "en": "which allows us to filter our service for their state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.01,
          "end": 10.62,
          "en": "And it seems to work great.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.62,
          "end": 13.59,
          "en": "We do have a certain issue with it though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.59,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "If we allow the user to add a new server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 19.29,
          "en": "and I will quickly add this functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.29,
          "end": 24.24,
          "en": "by going to my template and by adding a line break",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.24,
          "end": 25.41,
          "en": "and then a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.41,
          "end": 27.88,
          "en": "with the classes btn and btn-primary",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.19,
          "end": 30.81,
          "en": "where I say Add Server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.81,
          "end": 33.13,
          "en": "which will execute a new method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.98,
          "end": 37.83,
          "en": "onAddServer like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.83,
          "end": 39.03,
          "en": "And then in the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.03,
          "end": 41.493,
          "en": "I will quickly add this method onAddServer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.8,
          "end": 46.23,
          "en": "Here I will simply take my servers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.23,
          "end": 48.12,
          "en": "push a new server on it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.12,
          "end": 51.21,
          "en": "and, of course, this will just be a generic server here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.21,
          "end": 53.58,
          "en": "which will have the instance type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.58,
          "end": 55.86,
          "en": "of, let's say, small,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.86,
          "end": 60.48,
          "en": "a name of New Server, let's keep it super simple here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.48,
          "end": 65.48,
          "en": "a status of stable, and started could be new Date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.73,
          "end": 69.24,
          "en": "and then the same date as all the other servers here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.24,
          "end": 71.76,
          "en": "This is not the recording date, as a side note,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.76,
          "end": 75.15,
          "en": "just like or how the way you want it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.15,
          "end": 78.21000000000001,
          "en": "So with this, we are able to add a new server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.21000000000001,
          "end": 79.98,
          "en": "And if I now click on Add Server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.98,
          "end": 81.93,
          "en": "you see it's getting added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.93,
          "end": 85.02,
          "en": "If I filter for stable though, and I hit this button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.02,
          "end": 89.1,
          "en": "you don't see it getting added here, but it is there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.1,
          "end": 92.07,
          "en": "You can see if I removed the filter altogether.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.07,
          "end": 93.99000000000001,
          "en": "So I added a couple of servers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.99000000000001,
          "end": 96.3,
          "en": "and now we can filter for them again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.3,
          "end": 100.41,
          "en": "but they weren't added whilst we had this list filtered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.41,
          "end": 103.922,
          "en": "And this is actually not a bug.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.922,
          "end": 106.283,
          "en": "I'll quickly reload this and filter for stable again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.283,
          "end": 107.91,
          "en": "so that we can see this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.91,
          "end": 110.58,
          "en": "If I hit Enter here, as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.58,
          "end": 112.32,
          "en": "it's not getting added, but it's there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.32,
          "end": 115.25999999999999,
          "en": "We can see as soon as we clear our filter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.25999999999999,
          "end": 117.66,
          "en": "Now the reason for this behavior is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.66,
          "end": 120.93,
          "en": "that Angular is, thankfully, I should say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.93,
          "end": 123.75,
          "en": "not rerunning our pipe on the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.75,
          "end": 126.39,
          "en": "whenever this data changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 126.39,
          "end": 129.87,
          "en": "So as soon as we change what we enter here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.87,
          "end": 133.26,
          "en": "and even if we would only add a blank space",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.26,
          "end": 134.79,
          "en": "and then remove it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.79,
          "end": 138.24,
          "en": "we would update our pipe again, as you can see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.24,
          "end": 140.07,
          "en": "So adding the input, or excuse me,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 140.07,
          "end": 141.87,
          "en": "changing the input of the pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.87,
          "end": 144.747,
          "en": "will trigger a recalculation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.747,
          "end": 148.65,
          "en": "will trigger the pipe being applied to the data again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 148.65,
          "end": 151.5,
          "en": "But changing the data won't trigger this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 151.5,
          "end": 153.09,
          "en": "And this is a good behavior,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 156.81,
          "en": "because otherwise Angular would have to run this pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 156.81,
          "end": 161.52,
          "en": "or rerun this pipe whenever any data on the page changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 161.52,
          "end": 163.17000000000002,
          "en": "This would be really bad,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.17000000000002,
          "end": 165.63,
          "en": "because that would cost a lot of performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 165.63,
          "end": 167.57999999999998,
          "en": "And this is also the reason",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 167.57999999999998,
          "end": 170.97,
          "en": "why no built-in filter pipe exists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 170.97,
          "end": 175.07999999999998,
          "en": "because filtering, you would say, is a pretty common task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 175.07999999999998,
          "end": 178.17000000000002,
          "en": "But the Angular team decided against adding such a pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 178.17000000000002,
          "end": 181.47,
          "en": "because you typically have a high performance cost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 181.47,
          "end": 184.26,
          "en": "if you want to enforce it being updated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 184.26,
          "end": 186.87,
          "en": "even if you are in filter mode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 186.87,
          "end": 188.58,
          "en": "So, by default, it doesn't work here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 188.58,
          "end": 190.41,
          "en": "but we can force it to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 190.41,
          "end": 194.4,
          "en": "But again, be aware that the following change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 194.4,
          "end": 198.48,
          "en": "will make sure that whenever we change data on the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 198.48,
          "end": 202.5,
          "en": "our pipe is recalculated, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 202.5,
          "end": 205.17000000000002,
          "en": "So this might lead to performance issues.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 205.17000000000002,
          "end": 206.82,
          "en": "So you should know what you're doing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 206.82,
          "end": 209.43,
          "en": "which is why I'm really emphasizing this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 209.43,
          "end": 212.46,
          "en": "You can force this pipe to be updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 212.46,
          "end": 214.11,
          "en": "whenever the data changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 214.11,
          "end": 217.17000000000002,
          "en": "by adding a second property to the pipe decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 217.17000000000002,
          "end": 221.55,
          "en": "It's called pure, and you can set it to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 221.55,
          "end": 224.94,
          "en": "By default, this is true and doesn't need to be added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 224.94,
          "end": 228.06,
          "en": "Now if you do this and the app reloads,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 228.06,
          "end": 231.36,
          "en": "let's filter for stable servers and add new server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 231.36,
          "end": 234.06,
          "en": "And now you see they get added here too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 234.06,
          "end": 237.75,
          "en": "The reason simply is that the pipe now gets recalculated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 237.75,
          "end": 239.01,
          "en": "whenever data changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 239.01,
          "end": 240.15,
          "en": "And as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 240.15,
          "end": 242.25,
          "en": "this can lead to performance issues,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 242.25,
          "end": 244.35,
          "en": "but might be what you're interested in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 244.35,
          "end": 245.91,
          "en": "So it is fine to use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 245.91,
          "end": 248.73,
          "en": "this is what this pure property is there for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 248.73,
          "end": 250.23,
          "en": "You can set it to false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 250.23,
          "end": 252.54,
          "en": "which basically means this is not, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 252.54,
          "end": 257.54,
          "en": "purely focusing on whether the pipe arguments changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 257.58,
          "end": 259.95,
          "en": "but now it will also be recalculated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 259.95,
          "end": 262.11,
          "en": "whenever anything changes on the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 262.11,
          "end": 264.6,
          "en": "And again, this might be a bad behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 264.6,
          "end": 265.95,
          "en": "I'm just emphasizing this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 265.95,
          "end": 267.93,
          "en": "because it's so important to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 267.93,
          "end": 269.46,
          "en": "But if you know what you're doing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 269.46,
          "end": 271.02,
          "en": "if you do need this behavior,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 271.02,
          "end": 272.15999999999997,
          "en": "definitely go ahead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 272.15999999999997,
          "end": 275.52,
          "en": "set pure to false and you are good to go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 275.52,
          "end": 278.01,
          "en": "And with that, we now get a working filter pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 278.01,
          "end": 279.33,
          "en": "with this little downside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 279.33,
          "end": 281.67,
          "en": "of potentially hitting performance issues",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 281.67,
          "end": 283.83299999999997,
          "en": "if we have a very long list here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
